INT. PAWN SHOP - AFTER HOURS

Glass cases. Guitars on the wall. A wall of wristwatches ticking out of sync. One shattered window patched with cardboard.

DET. IRENE KOSTOPOULOS (50s, trench coat, tired eyes) crouches beside a broken display case, photographing the glass. OFFICER DAMIAN FOLASADE-REYES (20s, rookie, uniform too crisp) stands at the door writing in a notebook. SOL WEINBERG-ACHEBE (60s, shop owner, cardigan, hands behind his back) watches from behind the register. At the end of the counter, a teenager, JAMAL TEAGUE (17, hoodie, no shoes), sits cross-legged on the floor with a blanket around his shoulders.

Kostopoulos stands. Her knees crack. She nods at the broken case.

KOSTOPOULOS
What was in there?

SOL
Rings.

KOSTOPOULOS
How many?

SOL
Eleven.

She lifts one eyebrow. Sol studies the floor.

SOL (CONT'D)
Twelve.

KOSTOPOULOS
Mm.

Damian flips a page. Jamal pulls the blanket tighter. Kostopoulos crosses to him and lowers herself, stiffly, into a squat.

KOSTOPOULOS (CONT'D)
You got a name?

JAMAL
Jamal.

KOSTOPOULOS
Jamal. You hurt?

JAMAL
No.

KOSTOPOULOS
You hungry?

He shrugs. She looks up at Damian.

KOSTOPOULOS (CONT'D)
Officer. Find him something.

DAMIAN
Like what?

KOSTOPOULOS
Anything.

Damian leaves. Sol follows him with his eyes. The watches tick. Kostopoulos sits on the floor beside Jamal, her coat spreading around her.

KOSTOPOULOS (CONT'D)
Did you break the window?

JAMAL
It was already broken.

KOSTOPOULOS
Did you go in?

JAMAL
I was cold.

KOSTOPOULOS
That's not what I asked.

He shrugs again. Sol clears his throat.

SOL
He's been sleeping behind the dumpster for a week.

KOSTOPOULOS
You knew?

SOL
I leave the heater on in the back.

Kostopoulos looks at Sol, then at the boy. She exhales.

KOSTOPOULOS
So nobody broke in.

SOL
Somebody did. I just forgot to say hello.

Damian returns with a bag of crackers from the vending machine. Jamal takes it with both hands. Nobody mentions the twelve rings, and eventually Kostopoulos folds her notebook shut.
